## ECOPS resolution statuses

Jira has a limitation that prevents custom resolution names, so ECOPS tickets use proxy statuses. This app stores the **actual** meaning, not the Jira proxy. The full mapping:

| This app shows | Jira proxy | Meaning |
|----------------|------------|---------|
| Support Exception | Done-Errata | Deviation migrated to a formal Support Exception |
| Non-Impacting | Not a Bug | Deviation assessed as non-impacting to supportability |
| Corrected | Corrected | Deviation corrected — no longer deviates from RDS |
| Not a Deviation | Not a Deviation | Reviewed and determined to not be a deviation |

When referencing ticket resolutions in answers, always use the actual status (Support Exception, Non-Impacting, etc.), not the Jira proxy name.

